he should also bring in any facts she has not yet discussed, e.g., about other candidates. She could say she agrees with C but wants to compare with B's stress handling, etc. She must state her vote in metadata.\n\nProbably she should also vote for Candidate C, but provide additional perspective, maybe note that while C has communication issues, B's stress handling is strong but his communication tone is problematic. She could argue that C still best overall.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Sarah and James that Candidate C is the provisional recommendation. The reliability, quick decision-making, and positive crew atmosphere are critical. While communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are concerns, they are outweighed by the safety-critical strengths. Compared to B's stress handling, B's pretentiousness and tone issues raise crew cooperation concerns. A and D have leadership or responsibility issues. Therefore I also vote for Candidate C.\"\n\nMETADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
